course: dictionary
lesson: 7196
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Petal» is one of them. The words around it give the clues, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «Bright petals, scent and nectar, a sweet sugary juice, attract insects that carry pollen.» Here a petal is a thin, brightly coloured part of a flower. The clues are flower words such as nectar and pollen.
explain: Now read this: Mum sat on her bed and said, «Grown-ups split up for grown-up reasons, petal.» Petal is not a flower here. It is a friendly name, like «love» or «pet», that a grown-up uses for a child they care about. The clue is that Mum is speaking gently to someone she loves.
fact: A petal is one of the thin, often brightly coloured parts that make up the outer ring of a flower.
fact: Petals, scent and nectar attract insects such as bees and butterflies, which carry pollen.
fact: Many flowers have 3, 4, 5 or more petals.
fact: «Petal» is also a friendly name, used especially in the north of England, like «love» or «pet».
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «petal» means a flower part and the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
exercise: «Bright petals, scent and nectar attract insects that carry pollen.» In this sentence, what is a petal? | *A thin, brightly coloured part of a flower | A type of seed | A kind of insect | A friendly name for someone you love
exercise: Mum says, «Grown-ups split up for grown-up reasons, petal.» What does petal mean here? | A bright colour | *A friendly name, like «love» or «pet» | A bee | A flower part
exercise: «A flower has petals, stamens that make pollen and a carpel in the middle holding tiny ovules.» Which part holds the tiny ovules? | Petals | Stamens | Sepals | *Carpel
test: «Put a white carnation in a glass of water with blue ink: after a day its petals turn blue.» What happens to the petals? | They fall off at once | They turn into seeds | They stay white forever | *They turn blue after a day
test: «Every flower advertises to its own customers: bright colours and runway lines for bees.» Which creatures do bright colours attract here? | Hummingbirds only | Nobody at all | *Bees | Flies
exam: Sam says, «Thanks, petal!» to his nan. What does petal mean? | A flower part | A small insect | *A friendly name for someone you love | A bright colour
